# N2/STO-3G FCIQMC, SHORT run -- the S5 thread-count-invariance gate for the
# parallel spawn loop (docs/FCIQMC_PARALLEL_REWRITE_SCOPE.md, H2.1).
#
# WHY THIS EXISTS. h2_fciqmc_threads1/4 run on H2/STO-3G, whose 4 determinants
# are fewer than kBins=64, so at most one parent ever lands in a bin and a
# merge-order or cross-bin-annihilation defect can never surface there. This
# fixture is N2 (10 orbitals, 7a/7b, ndet=14400): a 500-step run reaches ~579
# occupied determinants, ~9 parents per bin, so two parents in different bins
# genuinely spawn onto the same child and the fixed-order merge is exercised.
#
# It is SHORT (300 equilibration + 200 sampling) purely so it fits the suite
# budget -- ~0.1 s per run. The energies are physically noisy (fixed-seed, but
# far from converged); that does not matter, because the S5 gate asserts
# BITWISE reproducibility of a deterministic trajectory, not physical accuracy.
# The physical validation of the method is n2_fciqmc_sto3g (the full 50k-step
# gate against exact FCI).
#
# The paired cases:
#   n2_fciqmc_s5_threads1  -- runs at OMP_NUM_THREADS=1, PINS both energies to
#                             fixed values (atol 0.0). This is the tripwire for
#                             a merge-order / accumulator-reassociation change
#                             that is thread-count-invariant but still alters
#                             the answer (verified at H2.1: reversing the
#                             bin-merge order moved the shift by ~0.26 Eh while
#                             T1==T4 still held, so only this pin caught it).
#                             The pinned values change legitimately whenever the
#                             accumulator's fold order or the RNG changes --
#                             H2.4 swapped unordered_map for SpawnAccumulator,
#                             H2.5 swapped mt19937_64 for xoshiro256**, each
#                             re-pinned. Not regressions; the FCI-agreement
#                             gates (n2_fciqmc_sto3g) guard the physics, this
#                             pins the byte-level determinism.
#   n2_fciqmc_s5_threads4  -- runs at OMP_NUM_THREADS=4, compares to threads1
#                             at atol 0.0. Tripwire for a partition that depends
#                             on thread count.
#
# Both are needed: neither catches the other's defect class.

%begin_control
    basis       sto-3g
    calculation energy
    verbosity   normal
    basis_type  cartesian
%end_control

%begin_scf
    scf_type    rhf
    correlation fciqmc
    ci_max_dim  200000

    fciqmc_walkers         10000
    fciqmc_timestep        0.001
    fciqmc_shift_damping   0.3
    fciqmc_shift_restoring 0.05
    fciqmc_shift_interval  5
    fciqmc_granularity     1.0
    fciqmc_initiator       0.0
    fciqmc_equilibration   300
    fciqmc_steps           200
    fciqmc_spawn_attempts  1
    fciqmc_seed            20250901

    use_diis    .true.
    diis_dim    8
    save_checkpoint .false.
    engine      os
    guess       hcore
%end_scf

%begin_geom
    coord_type  cartesian
    coord_units angstrom
    use_symm    .false.
%end_geom

%begin_coords
2
0   1
N     0.000000     0.000000     0.000000
N     0.000000     0.000000     1.098000
%end_coords
